From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 09:16:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02318/11362] [outer-loop] ARC gap-fill: structural-prompt +
 DECISIVE finding (cells != moves)

De-steered gap_fill_prompt from the Hamming default toward a structural
progress signal (use per-action deltas; mask static background; prefer a
move-distance proxy). Re-ran r11l: the LLM wrote a masked mismatch but A*
still found the 5-action path (not the optimal 3). A free heuristic_weight
sweep is decisive: NO weight gives r11l both the optimal 3-action path AND
fewer expansions than BFS (2236) -- at w=0.02 it's 3 acts but 2791 exp; at
w=1.0 it's 335 exp but 5 acts. The frontier is BFS-dominated at the optimal
end.

Root cause proven: CELLS != MOVES. One r11l click flips ~hundreds of cells,
so a cell-diff heuristic (1375 'wrong') is a terrible proxy for move-distance
(3). Cell-count helps ONLY in low-cell-impact games (su15, captured); in
high-cell-impact games (r11l/cn04/m0r0/sp80) it over-estimates -> greedy ->
suboptimal, and no weight rescues it. The real unlock is a MOVE-distance-
aware heuristic (actions-to-win, modelling per-action cell-impact) -- genuine
per-game research, flagged for a directed session. Honest stop: 1 clean
capture (su15) + the cell-count ceiling characterized and explained.
